      "id": 74699,
      "name": "Envisioner",
      "username": "Envisioner",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-09-30T00:15:22.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm no expert but I believe you did it right.&nbsp; The moment Blade is reduced to 0 HP, before anything else happens, he would normally be destroyed (there might be exceptions on cards which do something when destroyed, such as Ambuscade's Sonic Mine or Unity's Bee Bot; it's unclear exactly how long those stay in play and whether they can resolve their effects from the trash, but other cards definitely stop instantly when destroyed, we have a long-standing ruling about Visionary's Wrest the Mind which makes this definite).&nbsp; Flipping him to his second side replaces his destruction, and you would then resolve both Backlash Field and Flame Barrier.&nbsp; Note however that if Ra reduced the Baron below 0 HP with the original attack, the extra damage does not carry over to the Baron; he always heals up to 30 HP after flipping.&nbsp; This Flame Barrier interaction might be one of the promptest ways to start cutting him down again, though.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:54:47.444Z",
